    "narrative": "As we approach the final stretch of the season, our lineup efficiency is being severely tested by a heavy volume of team off-days for our core stars. Today, **Sam Antonacci** stands out as our premier start with a score of 58.38, buoyed primarily by his prime leadoff placement and a favorable platoon advantage against Blubaugh. While **Miguel Vargas** shares the same matchup in the heart of the order, his score of 50.48 is tempered by the park environment and marginal platoon splits. **Jackson Merrill** remains a solid option at 53.09; despite a challenging L/L matchup against the veteran Boyd, Merrill\u2019s recent form and order positioning keep his floor high enough to warrant a start in the outfield.\n\nOur bench decisions are largely dictated by a quiet schedule, with heavy hitters like **Kyle Tucker**, **Gunnar Henderson**, and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** inactive due to team off-days, while **Luis Robert Jr.** remains sidelined on the IL. Consequently, the fringe roster management is straightforward today; **Drake Baldwin** is our most interesting decision, garnering a 47.58 score. While his matchup against Luzardo is objectively tough given the pitcher's elite arm talent (3.06 xERA), **Drake Baldwin** earns the start at C1 primarily due to the lack of viable alternatives and the consistent output he provides at the top of the order. Similarly, **Heliot Ramos** rounds out our UTIL slot with a 46.77 score, benefiting from a park factor bump that helps mitigate the skill of Tolle on the mound. We are maintaining a conservative stance with the rest of our bench\u2014including **Andy Pages**, **Jordan Westburg**, and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**\u2014to preserve game caps for higher-leverage matchups as we close out the Roto standings.",
